      text: '13 of 23 North American assessment areas face elevated or high resource-adequacy risk over the next five years, with the highest risk in MISO, PJM, ERCOT and parts of the West. Data-center-driven demand growth threatens to outpace new resources; nearly every region is at elevated or high risk by 2030. NERC calls it "not a prediction of failure but an early warning on the trajectory of risk." (Critics funded by environmental groups argue utilities may double-count prospective demand.)',
