      text: 'A transmission fault in Northern Virginia caused about 1,500 MW of exclusively data-center load to disconnect on the customer side and switch to backup power. Operators had not anticipated it and voltage rose above normal levels. Reuters described it as roughly 60 data centers. NERC found reliability was not impacted this time but warned operators about the risk.',
